{"term":"reckon","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:661d4c8456a9a14246","definition":"To count; to enumerate; to number; also, to compute; to calculate.","example":"then the priest shall reckon unto him the money according to the years that remain","pos":"verb","synonyms":["number","enumerate","calculate","compute"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Commonwealth","register":"Commonwealth","wordFamily":["chinny reckon","dead reckon","forereckon","misreckon","outreckon","overreckon","reckonable","reckoner","reckon for","reckoning","reckonmaster","reckon on","reckon out","reckon up","reckon upon","reckon with","reckon without","reckon without one's host","to reckon with","underreckon","unreckoned","unreckoning"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e1655a18a9eae25935","definition":"To count as in a number, rank, or series; to estimate by rank or quality; to place by estimation; to account; to esteem; to repute.","example":"He was reckoned among the transgressors","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Commonwealth","register":"Commonwealth","wordFamily":["chinny reckon","dead reckon","forereckon","misreckon","outreckon","overreckon","reckonable","reckoner","reckon for","reckoning","reckonmaster","reckon on","reckon out","reckon up","reckon upon","reckon with","reckon without","reckon without one's host","to reckon with","underreckon","unreckoned","unreckoning"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7be01368c06d6ea4b","definition":"To charge, attribute, or adjudge to one, as having a certain quality or value.","example":"[…] faith was reckoned to Abraham for righteousness.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["value","rate","esteem"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Commonwealth","register":"Commonwealth","wordFamily":["chinny reckon","dead reckon","forereckon","misreckon","outreckon","overreckon","reckonable","reckoner","reckon for","reckoning","reckonmaster","reckon on","reckon out","reckon up","reckon upon","reckon with","reckon without","reckon without one's host","to reckon with","underreckon","unreckoned","unreckoning"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d7b1637d49b78ca2f5","definition":"To conclude, as by an enumeration and balancing of chances; hence, to think; to suppose; -- followed by an objective clause","example":"I reckon he won't try that again.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["think","believe","guess","suppose","esteem","figure"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Commonwealth, colloquial","register":"Commonwealth, colloquial","wordFamily":["chinny reckon","dead reckon","forereckon","misreckon","outreckon","overreckon","reckonable","reckoner","reckon for","reckoning","reckonmaster","reckon on","reckon out","reckon up","reckon upon","reckon with","reckon without","reckon without one's host","to reckon with","underreckon","unreckoned","unreckoning"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:301cf0cd51ca79f022","definition":"To reckon with something or somebody or not, i.e. to reckon without something or somebody: to take into account, deal with, consider or not, i.e. to misjudge, ignore, not take into account, not deal with, not consider or fail to consider; e.g. reckon without one's host","example":"There are hardships that nobody reckons;\nThere are valleys unpeopled and still;\nThere’s a land—oh, it beckons and beckons,\nAnd I want to go back—and I will.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"